 "background": "The song was composed by Sotir Dzingal. It describes an episode in which he and two other men from Ohrid took a boat they had rented from Vister and crossed the lake to Albania. Vister was a Viennese violinist who, with his family of musicians, played in the restaurants and hotels of Ohrid between the two world wars. Mood: nostalgic, a farewell to the home town and the mother.",
